===Etymology===
A post-classical word. Compare {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*l-tjwa||mouth; beak; food; stomach}}, whence {{cog|bo|ལྟོ་བ||stomach; belly}} (STEDT). Compare also {{cog|tai-pro|*dwuːŋꟲ||belly}} (whence {{cog|th|ท้อง}}) and {{cog|qfa-kms-pro|*luŋ²||stomach}}, as Middle Chinese ''shangsheng'' corresponds to foreign ''-ŋ'' in some words ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

Some dialects have different pronunciations for the two senses, "abdomen; belly (of a human)" and "stomach (of an animal)", derived from two different readings in Middle Chinese that differed in the voicing of the initial consonant.
* In Mandarin, the pronunciation for the former sense derives from the {{lang|zh|徒古切}} reading in Middle Chinese (i.e. the reading with voiced initial {{IPAchar|/d/}}) and the pronunciation for the latter sense derives from the {{lang|zh|當古切}} (i.e. the reading with voiceless initial {{IPAchar|/t/}}) reading.
* In Min Nan, the pronunciation for the former sense derives from the {{lang|zh|當古切}} reading and the pronunciation for latter sense derives from the {{lang|zh|徒古切}} reading.
* Cantonese uses the same pronunciation for both senses, derived from the {{lang|zh|徒古切}} reading.
* Hakka also uses the same pronunciation for both senses, but it is instead derived from the {{lang|zh|當古切}} reading.

