===Etymology===
Possibly from {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*tV-lak|*lak ~ *C-jak|arm; hand; wing}}. {{zh-ref|Sagart (1999)}} considers it to be a prefixed form of a root ''*lak'', found unprefixed as {{och-l|亦|tr=*ᵇlak|armpit}} and with a loosely attached prefix as ''*ᵃkə-lak'', preserved in some southern varieties, such as {{cog|yue|-}} {{zh-l|胳肋底|gaak3 laak6-1 dai2}}, {{cog|cdo|-}} {{zh-l|胳腋下|gó̤k-lŏ̤k-â}}. In the new reconstruction by {{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart (2014)}}, the connection to {{och-l|亦|tr=*[ɢ](r)Ak}} is still implied (cf. {{zh-ref|Sagart, 2007}}), but the comparison to the forms in the southern varieties no longer holds ({{zh-ref|Hill, 2019}}). {{zh-ref|Zhang, Jacques and Lai (2019)}} compare it with {{cog|bo|ལག||arm}}, {{cog|sit-jap|tɯ-jaʁ||arm}} and suggest that the comparisons are more compatible with an {{cog|och|-}} reconstruction such as ''*klˁak''.

Alternatively, {{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} reconstructs the {{cog|och|-}} minimally as ''*kâk'' < ''*klak'' and posits an {{der|zh|aav}} origin, comparing it to {{cog|mkh-mnc-pro|*knlak||popliteal space; armpit}}, {{cog|km|ក្លៀក||armpit}}, both from {{cog|mkh-pro|*kʔik|*kʔik ~ *kʔiək ~ *kʔaik|armpit}}.

